00,69,7,17,15,8,284,220,16,20,4779,12564,400,69,7,17,15,16,20,17,15,16,20,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f(x)$ be a function such that for all $x,$ $f(x) = f(x + 1) + f(x - 1).$  Given that $f(15) = 20$ and $f(20) = 15,$ compute $f(20152015).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3a06947d31691cba40d873bfa71381aed6cb94523de23cfa4a624a1607c9fd49"},"seconds":59.11891508102417,"seed":725726030558183082,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the functional equation given: \\( f(x) = f(x + 1) + f(x - 1) \\). This equation suggests a recurrence relation that we can use to find a pattern or solve for specific values of \\( f(x) \\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the equation in terms of a sequence. Define \\( a_n = f(n) \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\\[ a_n = a_{n+1} + a_{n-1}. \\]\nRearranging, we get:\n\\[ a_{n+1} = a_n - a_{n-1}. \\]\n\nWe are given two specific values: \\( a_{15} = 20 \\) and \\( a_{20} = 15 \\). To find a pattern, we need to compute a few more terms. Let's denote \\( a_{14} = a \\) and \\( a_{16} = b \\). Using the recurrence relation, we have:\n\\[ a_{15} = a_{16} + a_{14} \\implies 20 = b + a \\implies b = 20 - a. \\]\n\\[ a_{16} = a_{15} - a_{14} \\implies b = 20 - a. \\]\n\\[ a_{17} = a_{16} - a_{15} = (20 - a) - 20 = -a. \\]\n\\[ a_{18} = a_{17} - a_{16} = -a - (20 - a) = -20. \\]\n\\[ a_{19} = a_{18} - a_{17} = -20 - (-a) = -20 + a. \\]\n\\[ a_{20} = a_{19} - a_{18} = (-20 + a) - (-20) = a. \\]\nWe know \\( a_{20} = 15 \\), so \\( a = 15 \\). Now we can find \\( b \\):\n\\[ b = 20 - a = 20 - 15 = 5. \\]\nSo, the sequence starts as:\n\\[ a_{14} = 15, \\, a_{15} = 20, \\, a_{16} = 5, \\, a_{17} = -15, \\, a_{18} = -20, \\, a_{19} = -5, \\, a_{20} = 15, \\, a_{21} = 20, \\, a_{22} = 5, \\, \\ldots \\]\nWe observe that the sequence repeats every 6 terms. To confirm, we can check:\n\\[ a_{21} = a_{20} - a_{19} = 15 - (-5) = 20, \\]\n\\[ a_{22} = a_{21} - a_{20} = 20 - 15 = 5, \\]\n\\[ a_{23} = a_{22} - a_{21} = 5 - 20 = -15, \\]\n\\[ a_{24} = a_{23} - a_{22} = -15 - 5 = -20, \\]\n\\[ a_{25} = a_{24} - a_{23} = -20 - (-15) = -5, \\]\n\\[ a_{26} = a_{25} - a_{24} = -5 - (-20) = 15. \\]\nThe sequence indeed repeats every 6 terms. Therefore, to find \\( a_{20152015} \\), we need to find the position of 20152015 in the repeating cycle. We compute:\n\\[ 20152015 \\mod 6 = 5. \\]\nSo, \\( a_{20152015} = a_5 \\). From our sequence, we see that \\( a_5 = -5 \\).\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(20152015) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-5}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
